WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.510
Last time we explored a finished planner.

2
00:00:02.577 --> 00:00:06.830
This time we start with an empty
page and make something of our own:

3
00:00:06.830 --> 00:00:09.207
the cover of a family recipe book.

4
00:00:09.275 --> 00:00:14.275
Along the way you'll meet every drawing
tool, and the few rules the canvas plays by.

5
00:00:14.502 --> 00:00:18.112
This is a fresh, blank
project: one A4 page.

6
00:00:18.183 --> 00:00:19.463
First, a name.

7
00:00:19.552 --> 00:00:24.431
The tab takes its name from the top
page, so I'll call it Family Recipes.

8
00:00:24.638 --> 00:00:28.238
And I'll zoom out one step, so
the whole page fits on screen.

9
00:00:28.443 --> 00:00:30.383
Across the top are the tools.

10
00:00:30.446 --> 00:00:32.686
Select, and the hand, for panning.

11
00:00:32.741 --> 00:00:37.092
Then text, rectangle, ellipse,
triangle, line, and the data grid,

12
00:00:37.092 --> 00:00:39.551
which gets an episode of its own.

13
00:00:39.627 --> 00:00:42.127
Each one has a single-letter shortcut.

14
00:00:42.335 --> 00:00:44.255
Press R for the rectangle.

15
00:00:44.364 --> 00:00:47.784
Now, here's the rule that
catches everyone the first time.

16
00:00:47.915 --> 00:00:49.865
A single click draws nothing.

17
00:00:49.983 --> 00:00:51.363
You have to drag.

18
00:00:51.569 --> 00:00:54.699
Press, drag to the opposite
corner, and let go.

19
00:00:55.264 --> 00:01:00.360
The tool stays active after you draw, so
dragging again makes a second rectangle,

20
00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:01.994
not a moved first one.

21
00:01:02.089 --> 00:01:03.929
Control Z takes it back.

22
00:01:04.135 --> 00:01:07.525
Press V for the select tool,
and click the rectangle.

23
00:01:07.631 --> 00:01:11.300
You get eight handles for
resizing, a rotate handle on top,

24
00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:15.281
and this small dot in the middle:
the pivot it turns around.

25
00:01:15.487 --> 00:01:16.957
Drag it to move it.

26
00:01:17.095 --> 00:01:21.325
The arrow keys nudge it one point
at a time, or ten with Shift held.

27
00:01:21.533 --> 00:01:25.485
For exact numbers, Geometry, on
the right, takes typed values.

28
00:01:25.598 --> 00:01:31.937
I want this card 24 points in
from every edge: X and Y of 24,

29
00:01:31.937 --> 00:01:35.928
a width of 547, and a height of 794.

30
00:01:36.133 --> 00:01:37.273
Now the look.

31
00:01:37.389 --> 00:01:39.629
Fill can be a color, or a pattern.

32
00:01:39.746 --> 00:01:43.336
I'll switch it to Pattern, choose
Dots, and pick a soft peach.

33
00:01:46.109 --> 00:01:49.299
That's dot grid paper,
made from one rectangle.

34
00:01:49.402 --> 00:01:54.509
The PDF stores it as a single repeating
pattern rather than thousands of dots,

35
00:01:54.509 --> 00:01:56.331
so the file stays small.

36
00:01:56.536 --> 00:02:00.189
For the border, a darker orange,
two points wide, and dashed.

37
00:02:00.324 --> 00:02:02.742
And Radius rounds the corners off.

38
00:02:06.308 --> 00:02:07.868
Press T for text.

39
00:02:08.017 --> 00:02:11.833
Text is the one tool where a
single click does make something:

40
00:02:11.833 --> 00:02:14.237
a small box that grows as you type.

41
00:02:14.307 --> 00:02:18.627
For a title, though, I'd rather drag out
the full width, so it stays centered.

42
00:02:18.845 --> 00:02:21.055
Type the title, then press Escape.

43
00:02:21.160 --> 00:02:24.700
That commits the text and drops
you back to the select tool.

44
00:02:24.906 --> 00:02:26.816
The font picker is searchable.

45
00:02:26.932 --> 00:02:29.602
I'll type play, and take Playfair Display.

46
00:02:29.704 --> 00:02:33.124
After that, a bigger size,
bold, and a deep brown.

47
00:02:36.551 --> 00:02:39.271
Now a subtitle, dragged out the same way.

48
00:02:39.324 --> 00:02:43.670
Notice it starts with the same
font, size and color as the title.

49
00:02:43.781 --> 00:02:46.191
The text tool remembers
your last settings.

50
00:02:46.305 --> 00:02:51.405
This one needs to be smaller, so 18
points, and italic instead of bold.

51
00:02:51.612 --> 00:02:53.752
A circle for a little decoration.

52
00:02:53.825 --> 00:02:58.375
E for ellipse, and hold Shift as you
drag, to keep it perfectly round.

53
00:02:58.581 --> 00:03:00.991
A solid peach fill, and no border.

54
00:03:03.448 --> 00:03:05.408
And a short line under the title.

55
00:03:05.440 --> 00:03:07.752
L for line, and drag it across.

56
00:03:12.061 --> 00:03:13.711
Is everything centered?

57
00:03:13.866 --> 00:03:15.016
Not quite.

58
00:03:15.094 --> 00:03:18.508
I'll select it all by dragging
a box from outside the page,

59
00:03:18.508 --> 00:03:21.594
and the toolbar grows a
row of alignment buttons.

60
00:03:21.724 --> 00:03:26.143
Align Center lines up every middle,
halfway between the outermost edges,

61
00:03:26.143 --> 00:03:27.990
which here are the card's.

62
00:03:28.202 --> 00:03:30.922
To look closer, hold Control and scroll.

63
00:03:31.062 --> 00:03:33.762
The zoom centers on
wherever the pointer is.

64
00:03:33.848 --> 00:03:39.044
The hand tool, H, drags the view around,
and so does holding down the middle mouse

65
00:03:39.044 --> 00:03:39.738
button.

66
00:03:39.946 --> 00:03:43.685
The magnet turns on snapping,
and shows the grid it snaps to.

67
00:03:43.762 --> 00:03:48.242
The grid gets finer as you zoom in, so
it doesn't fight you on detail work.

68
00:03:48.299 --> 00:03:50.079
I'll switch both off again.

69
00:03:52.242 --> 00:03:57.642
If anything goes wrong, Control Z steps
back, and Control Y steps forward again.

70
00:03:57.742 --> 00:04:00.042
And there is no save button to forget.

71
00:04:00.095 --> 00:04:04.045
This badge shows the project is
saved in your browser as you work.

72
00:04:04.252 --> 00:04:06.152
Let's see it as a PDF.

73
00:04:09.656 --> 00:04:12.179
One page, exactly as designed.

74
00:04:12.283 --> 00:04:16.811
In the next episode, we turn this
cover into a whole recipe notebook,

75
00:04:16.811 --> 00:04:20.683
with a page template that fills
itself in for every recipe.
